<title>AUSTRALIA: British Aerospace adds to missile decoy deal.</title>
<headline>British Aerospace adds to missile decoy deal.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian government said on Thursday that British Aerospace Plc's Australian subsidiary would supply Australia, the United States, and Canada with decoy rounds for its Nulka naval missile decoy system under a A$114 million contract.</p>
<p>The rounds would be delivered from late 1998 and the overall Nulka systems shold be operationsal from mid-1999.</p>
<p>Nulka, which was designed as a joint venture betweent he Australian and U.S. navies, fires hovering rockets which lure anti-ship missiles away from their targets.  </p>
<p>British Aerospace Australia said 10 days ago that it had a contract to supply the Nulka system to Canada.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
